---
// Design review page: the proposed standard type styles (H1 to H4, P1 to P4). Not part of the site: remove before launch.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const styles = [
  { id: 'h1', name: 'H1', size: '40 / 32', weight: 'Bold 700', lh: '1.15', use: 'Page titles (Upcoming Workshops, Upcoming Events, Writings, Lectures, Shows, Blog, Contact, workshop pages), and the "Past Workshops" / "Past Events" headings, which are H2 elements shown at H1 size.', sample: 'Upcoming Workshops', cls: 's-h1' },
  { id: 'h2', name: 'H2', size: '32 / 24', weight: 'Bold 700', lh: '1.25', use: 'Section headings inside a page (headings in the text of workshop pages and blog posts).', sample: 'Running text', cls: 's-h2' },
  { id: 'h3', name: 'H3', size: '24 / 18', weight: 'Bold 700', lh: '1.25', use: 'Item titles: workshop titles and event titles in the lists, sub-sections.', sample: 'Red Nose Intensive', cls: 's-h3' },
  { id: 'p1', name: 'P1', size: '18 / 18', weight: 'Regular 400', lh: '1.6', use: 'All running text, bio, descriptions, lists, subtitles.', sample: 'Clown is about comic poetry: funny and touching, essential and rigorous. Deeply rooted in movement-based theater, this workshop proposes an intensive training in Red Nose Theater Clown.', cls: 's-p1' },
  { id: 'p2', name: 'P2', size: '16 / 16', weight: 'Regular 400, grey', lh: '1.6', use: 'Places, notes, collaborators, dates and details in lists, year labels, blog list dates and categories.', sample: 'Padova, Italy · Helikos Studio · with Zsófi Kigyóssy', cls: 's-p2' },
  { id: 'p3', name: 'P3', size: '14 / 14', weight: 'Regular 400, grey', lh: '1.6', use: 'Notices ("this text is in English"), photo captions, form hints.', sample: 'Questo testo è in inglese. La versione italiana non è ancora disponibile.', cls: 's-p3' },
  { id: 'nav', name: 'Menu and language toggle (not part of the set)', size: '16', weight: 'Semibold 600, current page bold 700, UPPERCASE, spaced .08em', lh: '1.6', use: 'The main menu, the Creations dropdown and the language toggle (they always match).', sample: 'ABOUT  WORKSHOPS  EVENTS  CREATIONS  CONTACT', cls: 's-nav' },
];
---
<Base title="Type system review" lang="en" path="/design/type-system/" noindex wide>
  <h1>Type system: the standard styles (applied 261009)</h1>
  <p>Sizes are <strong>desktop / phone</strong> in pixels. Everything is Figtree. Almost all of it is what the site already uses; the changes are called out below the table. Use the buttons to see the samples at phone sizes.</p>
  <div class="tsys-btns" role="group" aria-label="Sizes"><button type="button" data-mode="desktop" aria-pressed="true">Desktop sizes</button><button type="button" data-mode="phone" aria-pressed="false">Phone sizes</button></div>

  <div id="tsys">
    {styles.map((s) => (
      <section class="tsys-row">
        <div class="tsys-meta">
          <h2 class="tsys-name">{s.name}</h2>
          <dl>
            <dt>Size</dt><dd>{s.size}</dd>
            <dt>Weight</dt><dd>{s.weight}</dd>
            <dt>Line spacing</dt><dd>{s.lh}</dd>
            <dt>Used for</dt><dd>{s.use}</dd>
          </dl>
        </div>
        <div class="tsys-sample"><p class={s.cls}>{s.sample}</p></div>
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>There is no H4 and no P4. The poem on the landing page (22px), the About page's signature block, and the menu are their own styles outside this set.</li>
    <li>In the stylesheet these are variables (<code>--h1-size</code> to <code>--p3-size</code>) and classes (<code>.h1</code> to <code>.h3</code>, <code>.p1</code> to <code>.p3</code>); phone sizes step down in one place.</li>
  </ul>

  <script is:inline>
    var root = document.getElementById('tsys');
    document.querySelectorAll('.tsys-btns button').forEach(function (b) {
      b.addEventListener('click', function () {
        document.querySelectorAll('.tsys-btns button').forEach(function (x) { x.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(x === b)); });
        root.classList.toggle('phone', b.dataset.mode === 'phone');
      });
    });
  </script>

  <style is:global>
    .tsys-btns { display: flex; gap: .5rem; margin: 1rem 0 2rem; }
    .tsys-btns button { font: inherit; padding: .4rem 1rem; border: 1px solid #000; background: #fff; color: #000; border-radius: 999px; cursor: pointer; }
    .tsys-btns button[aria-pressed="true"] { background: #000; color: #fff; }
    .tsys-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(14rem, 22rem) 1fr; gap: 1.5rem 2.5rem; padding: 1.5rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); align-items: start; }
    @media (max-width: 52rem) { .tsys-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
    .tsys-name { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
    .tsys-meta dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: .15rem 1rem; margin: 0; font-size: .95rem; }
    .tsys-meta dt { color: var(--muted); }
    .tsys-meta dd { margin: 0; }
    .tsys-sample p { margin: 0; }
    .s-h1 { font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.15; }
    .s-h2 { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.25; }
    .s-h3 { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.25; }
    .s-p1 { font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 44rem; }
    .s-p2 { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted); }
    .s-p3 { font-size: .875rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted); }
    .s-nav { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; }
    #tsys.phone .s-h1 { font-size: 2rem; }
    #tsys.phone .s-h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; }
    #tsys.phone .s-h3 { font-size: 1.125rem; }
  </style>
</Base>
